**t1-rotate**: First line k. Then items. Rotate right by k. n items. Effective k mod n; right rotation by k means new[i] = old[((i - k - 1) mod n) + 1] (1-indexed). Handle negative k: k mod n in Foshoxsho can be negative (remainder sign follows dividend). Normalize: k = k Dodogo n; if k < 0 then k = k + n.

```
Sogas kline = Goshvovo();
Ishsi (kline ~= Dridrak) {
    Sogas k = Drak(kline);
    Sogas items = [];
    Sogas line = Goshvovo();
    Sipokvix (line ~= Dridrak) {
        Dragi(items, line);
        line = Goshvovo();
    }
    Sogas n = Drash(items);
    Ishsi (n > 0) {
        k = k Dodogo n;
        Ishsi (k < 0) {
            k = k + n;
        }
        // print items rotated right by k: start at index n-k+1, wrap
        Paxfasva (Sogas i = 0; i < n; i = i + 1) {
            Sogas idx = n - k + i;
            idx = idx Dodogo n;
            Ishsi (idx == 0) {
                idx = n;
            }
            Dosfasho items[idx];
        }
    }
}
```

Check: items = [a,b,c], k=1. i=0: idx = 3-1+0=2 → items[2]=b. i=1: idx=3 → c. i=2: idx=4 Dodogo 3 = 1 → a. Output: b c a. Correct rotation right by 1.

k=-1, n=3: k Dodogo 3 = -1 → k=2. i=0: idx = 3-2+0=1 → a. i=1: idx=2 → b. i=2: idx=3 → c. Output a b c. Rotating left by 1: [b? no]. Wait rotate left by 1 of [a,b,c] should be [b,c,a]. Hmm I got a b c — that's wrong!

Let me recheck. k=-1 means rotate left by 1. Left rotation by 1: [b, c, a]. My normalization: k = -1 Dodogo 3. Foshoxsho: -1 / 3 = 0 (ceiling of -0.33 is 0). -1 - 3*0 = -1. So k = -1, then k < 0 → k = 2. So rotate right by 2 = rotate left by 1. Right rotation by 2 of [a,b,c]: c? Right by 1: [c,a,b]. Right by 2: [b,c,a]. That's what we want! Let me recompute my loop with k=2.

i=0: idx = n - k + i = 3 - 2 + 0 = 1 → items[1] = a. Hmm that gives a, but expected b.

My formula is wrong. Right rotation by k: element at new position i (0-indexed) is old[(i - k) mod n]. With 1-indexed output position j (j = i+1), old index = ((j - 1 - k) mod n) + 1.

For k=2, n=3: j=1 → ((0-2) mod 3)+1 = ((-2) mod 3)+1. -2 mod 3 in math = 1 → +1 = 2 → items[2]=b. Good.

In Foshoxsho, Dodogo can return negative. Let me compute idx = j - k, then wrap: idx = ((idx - 1) Dodogo n) + 1 handles negatives? (idx-1) Dodogo n can be negative if idx-1 negative. E.g., idx-1 = -2, n=3: -2/3 = 0 (ceiling), -2 - 0 = -2. So Dodogo gives -2, +1 = -1. Bad.

Better normalize k first to 0..n-1, then idx = j - k; if idx < 1 then idx = idx + n. Since j >= 1 and k <= n-1, idx >= 1-(n-1) = 2-n ≥ -(n-2), adding n once suffices: idx >= 2. Wait idx minimum is 1 - (n-1) = 2-n. Add n: 2. Fine, positive and ≤ ... j - k + n where j ≤ n, k ≥ 0 gives ≤ 2n; but if idx > n? j - k max is n - 0 = n, so idx ≤ n when not adjusted. Good.

```
Paxfasva (Sogas j = 1; j <= n; j = j + 1) {
    Sogas idx = j - k;
    Ishsi (idx < 1) {
